WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.277
Load balancing multiple local LLM servers can improve total request throughput, availability, and workflow flexibility.

2
00:00:08.277 --> 00:00:15.056
It gives tools one stable endpoint while backend servers can be added, removed, repaired, or resized.

3
00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:28.772
The durable expectation is simple: ordinary load balancing routes requests across independently running endpoints; it does not automatically combine machines into one faster single inference session.

4
00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:32.556
A reliable setup depends on understanding each backend.

5
00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:42.488
Hardware resources, model files, runtime settings, context length, API compatibility, streaming behavior, and failure modes all shape capacity.

6
00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:45.011
Routing should reflect that reality.

7
00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:57.939
Round-robin may be enough for similar servers, while weighted, least-connections, health-check, model-aware, queue-based, and failover strategies become important as workloads diverge.

8
00:00:57.939 --> 00:01:01.013
Workload awareness keeps the service usable.

9
00:01:01.013 --> 00:01:14.571
Interactive chat, coding agents, batch summarization, document analysis, embeddings, long-context requests, and tool-using workflows have different latency, state, retry, and concurrency needs.

10
00:01:14.571 --> 00:01:18.907
Sticky sessions may matter when state or cache behavior matters.

11
00:01:18.907 --> 00:01:23.164
Stateless requests may route freely to any compatible backend.

12
00:01:23.164 --> 00:01:26.238
Operations and security complete the design.

13
00:01:26.238 --> 00:01:40.742
Measure real workloads, monitor the gateway and every backend, watch queue growth and failures, preserve streaming behavior, and troubleshoot mismatches in model names, runtime versions, endpoints, and timeouts.

14
00:01:40.742 --> 00:01:48.467
Protect local LLM endpoints because they may process sensitive prompts, documents, source code, and tool outputs.

15
00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:54.537
The goal is a practical local inference service that is measured, reliable, and safe to use.
